Surprise-gated action batches for the ARC-AGI-3 Duck harness
==============================================================

Our own code in this directory (surprise_gate.py, surprise_predicates.py, the
tests, scripts and docs, and the lines this patch adds) is released under MIT-0
(see LICENSE), as the ARC Prize 2026 rules require for code we author.

surprise-gate.patch modifies three files of a third-party code base. Those
files remain under their original licences; the patch adds a modification
notice at the top of each, as Apache-2.0 section 4(b) requires:

  * ARC-AGI-3 Milestone 2 solution, Copyright Daniel Franzen
    https://github.com/da-fr/arc-agi-3-solution - Apache License 2.0
    (LICENSE in that repository). The patch applies on top of his harness
    patch / repository state (upstream Duck commit 7652836 + his changes).
  * "Duck" harness (ARC3-Inference) and TAAF framework, Copyright Jeroen
    Cottaar / Tufa Labs - https://github.com/Tufalabs/duck-harness
    Code: MIT; Kaggle notebook: Apache-2.0 (per the authors' statement in
    https://www.kaggle.com/competitions/arc-prize-2026-arc-agi-3/discussion/717133;
    the GitHub repository itself carries no LICENSE file).

The public ARC-AGI-3 game files used by tests/test_public_games.py are NOT
included; tests/fetch_public_games.py downloads them from ARC Prize with the
toolkit's free anonymous key.
